https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TNpLSaCirj8  (Capo 2)

There's also a version in G with (G) and (C) . . . uh, just because.

TIP:  Super easy song with just two chords but there's a distinct rhythm that goes from beginning to end.  You'll pick it up immediately.

TIP:  Take a look at the instrumental bridge.  See that lonely (A5) in place of an (A) in the fourth couplet?  There's a little treble zing to that (A).  You can play the (A) like an (F5) but in this case I think playing the barre is easier since you already have two fingers in the 2nd fret from the preceding (D) and you can just collapse down onto the 2nd fret with your index finger and then extend your pinky over to the 5th fret.  Of course if you just don't want to deal with it just play a regular (A). 


